WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.680
A single gene is a tiny fraction of a genome.

2
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:13.460
Before cloning, it was rarely possible to get enough of one gene to cut, sequence or

3
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:19.960
study. So how do you pull one chosen gene out of a mixture of thousands, grow it as

4
00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:21.820
a pure clone, and read it?

5
00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:26.790
Restriction enzymes cut DNA at defined sequences.

6
00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:35.730
EcoRI cuts GAATTC, leaving single-stranded overhangs that pair with any

7
00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:40.890
other EcoRI end. So cut plasmid and insert fit together.

8
00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:43.950
DNA ligase then seals them.

9
00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:47.090
A living cell must still copy the result.

10
00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:53.453
A plasmid vector has an origin of replication, a selectable marker such as

11
00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:56.093
ampicillin resistance, and a cloning site.

12
00:00:57.193 --> 00:01:02.593
Cold calcium chloride makes bacteria competent to take up the plasmid, though only a

13
00:01:02.593 --> 00:01:07.653
fraction do. Antibiotic leaves only the cells that carry the plasmid.

14
00:01:08.713 --> 00:01:13.113
In a blue-white screen, the cloning site sits inside lacZ-alpha.

15
00:01:13.753 --> 00:01:17.593
Intact, it helps make an enzyme that turns X-gal blue.

16
00:01:18.393 --> 00:01:21.133
An insert breaks it, so the colony is white.

17
00:01:21.917 --> 00:01:25.657
One route to a gene starts from its messenger RNA.

18
00:01:26.757 --> 00:01:32.977
Reverse transcriptase copies it into complementary DNA, or cDNA, and the double-

19
00:01:32.977 --> 00:01:34.537
stranded copy is cloned.

20
00:01:35.237 --> 00:01:40.377
A tissue rich in that messenger, such as a ray's electric organ, makes the clone

21
00:01:40.377 --> 00:01:46.377
more common. Colonies on a filter are broken open, their DNA is fixed to the filter,

22
00:01:46.557 --> 00:01:49.517
and a labeled probe pairs with the wanted clone.

23
00:01:49.517 --> 00:01:55.557
The probe can be a related gene, an oligonucleotide from partial protein sequence,

24
00:01:55.957 --> 00:01:59.397
or, if the library expresses the protein, an antibody.

25
00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:03.730
A radioactive probe exposes X-ray film.

26
00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:09.710
Dark spots mark colonies whose DNA pairs with the probe, matched to a reference

27
00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:14.630
plate. White colonies are a strong hint of an insert, not proof.

28
00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:20.470
Estrogen receptor clones were found with an antibody and with oligonucleotide

29
00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:24.450
probes. The full cDNA gave the protein sequence.

30
00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:29.650
Expressed in HeLa cells, it bound estradiol like the natural receptor.

31
00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:35.523
Antibiotic resistance and color are traits, not sequence.

32
00:02:36.063 --> 00:02:41.703
A vector that closed without an insert still gives resistant colonies, so plate a

33
00:02:41.703 --> 00:02:44.403
vector-only ligation to measure that background.

34
00:02:45.283 --> 00:02:47.803
Some white colonies carry no insert.

35
00:02:48.143 --> 00:02:53.203
So confirm by digest or colony PCR, and sequence both junctions.

36
00:02:54.243 --> 00:03:00.783
Clones can lose DNA or be incomplete, so compare the insert with its expected size.

37
00:03:00.783 --> 00:03:09.583
In 1973, Cohen, Chang, Boyer and Helling made recombinant plasmids that replicate in

38
00:03:09.583 --> 00:03:18.863
E. coli. In 1982, Noda, Numa and colleagues read the 461 amino acids of the Torpedo

39
00:03:18.863 --> 00:03:23.823
acetylcholine receptor alpha-subunit precursor from cloned cDNA.

40
00:03:25.263 --> 00:03:28.083
Cloning gave the sequence from the gene, not the protein.

41
00:03:28.967 --> 00:03:37.827
In 1986, Nathans, Thomas and Hogness cloned human red, green and blue pigment genes.

42
00:03:38.767 --> 00:03:44.067
A first screen with the bovine rhodopsin probe found only human rhodopsin.

43
00:03:44.907 --> 00:03:49.447
The cone genes appeared when hybridization was relaxed to allow mismatches.

44
00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:53.727
A probe may find only the gene you already know.

45
00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.507
Color and resistance are hints.

46
00:03:56.507 --> 00:03:58.847
Sequence confirms a clone.
